{
  "name": "terminal-minimal-patch-redelivery",
  "purpose": "The comparison basis for a terminal restatement is the patch, not the record: only the members the event carries are compared, and the ones it omits are not differences. An activity terminalized by the minimal patch — activityId and state, nothing else — whose identical minimal content arrives again at the next sequence is therefore a no-op, even though the record still holds the kind, cause, origin turn, run, and progress that first sight established and this delivery never mentions. The redelivery is a new sequence rather than a reused identity, so it is not the exact-retransmission rule doing the work: a reducer that reads omission as erasure, or that judges the whole record instead of the patch, refuses a stream that said nothing new.",
  "negotiated": {
    "versions": [1],
    "updatesOutsidePrompt": true,
    "authoritativeQuiescence": true,
    "quiescenceSource": "process-containment",
    "activityKinds": ["task", "subagent"]
  },
